          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-342490/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "source": "sections/sec-004-2-storage-conditions-and-shelf-life-of-vaccine.md",
      "source_hash": "54b899b0cb9440bd7c41779a5cc01224dcea1b3d682e00a2d9c96160636b005c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out storage conditions and shelf life for the Janssen COVID-19 vaccine, frozen for up to 24 months or refrigerated for up to 4.5 months, and stresses protection from light and no refreezing after thawing. It explains that opened vials must be used within six hours or by the end of the session, and how to record dates and update expiry dates when moving vials to the refrigerator.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-342490/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "source": "sections/sec-005-thawing-of-frozen-vaccine.md",
      "source_hash": "4d7c3c18c3e262e329f44df59fab10d4cc1bee1ddc67e145257acdd88ae025fb",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that frozen vials can be thawed in the refrigerator, taking about two hours for one vial and twelve for a carton, and must not be refrozen.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
